      },
      "text": "Panama from coast to coast: national parks, islands and valleys"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:lead:e3456bc1f4d270f4",
      "field": "lead",
      "sourceTextSha256": "63579609ca80f242cb2098d22d44941715a02e90f0a575423fc44a2ab88f9915",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-97d3eeec2bfb-mw9olsy5",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "This seven-day itinerary takes in several very different sides of Panama. Explore the modern capital and the ruins of the old city, visit an Emberá village in Chagres National Park and cross to Taboga Island in the Pacific. The route also takes in the forests of Soberanía, Fort San Lorenzo and the Panama Canal locks before heading to El Valle de Antón, a town inside a volcanic caldera."
